	This is a question I have been puzzling over for quite some
time now.  I am wondering if some of you can define "nethack abuse".
I see references to it all the time in articles posted here, but I
have never seen a canonical list.  I am also interested in *WHY* each
thing is considered an abuse.  Some things are more clear than others
like backing up save files to save you from dying of stupidity or so
that you can identify everything and then go back and restart the game.
The ones I am interested in are the "abuses" like polypiling or 
stealing from shops.  I don't understand why these are necessarily
abuses, yet I see people write things like: "...I didn't have any
non-abusive ways to rip off the shop..." or "... I ascended with nnnn
points, and I DIDNT EVEN POLYPILE ONCE!...".  I can also see it if 
there is a bug in the code that people exploit (such as the infamous
"bag of infinite holding" bug) but why is it that when someone figures
out a way to use the items tp gain a bigger than expected advantage,
it is called abuse?  Sorry if I rambled too much.  I am not a Nethack
cheat...  it would take the fun out of the game.  I would like to hear
from you though on what is considered abuse and why.  Please e-mail me
and I will summarize to the net later.  If the mail bounces, wait a day
and try again.  We have been having some difficulties over the last couple
of weeks.

